    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (76.67) and **Bryson Stott** (72.46) represent our offensive foundation. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is the clear top play, overcoming a matchup against a quality arm in Rod\u00f3n by leveraging an excellent batting order position and solid platoon efficiency. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** draws a favorable matchup against Scherzer; despite the opposing pitcher's pedigree, the underlying metrics and a strong platoon edge boost his efficiency well into the elite tier. **Lawrence Butler** is also worth noting as a high-upside play at 66.94; even with the lineup status pending, he benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Sproat, making him a prime candidate for a breakout performance if he retains his assumed spot in the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Geraldo Perdomo**, who landed at 44.86, narrowly missing the cutoff for the utility slot. While **Geraldo Perdomo** provides the speed we covet in our 5x5 Roto build, he was edged out by the superior power-projection of the active starters against their respective opponents. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** (44.02) was relegated to the bench due to a combination of a challenging matchup against Warren and a 41% rain risk, which adds unnecessary volatility. Elsewhere, the lineup looks stable, though we are monitoring **Taylor Ward** (55.54) closely; his score is heavily buoyed by a +16% park factor despite a tough draw against George Kirby. We remain without the services of **Cal Raleigh** and **Will Smith**, forcing us to rely on our active depth to keep pace in categories where we are currently thin.",
